---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LEGAL, SITE_URL, LANG_TAGS } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { label } from '../../i18n/nav';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
/** Date de la dernière réécriture de cette page (aucun cookie, Clarity en mode sans cookie). */
const updated = displayDate('2026-10-06', LANG_TAGS[lang]);
const title = 'Salary Calculator Privacy in Greece: Data, No Cookies';
const description = 'Greek salary calculator privacy: your figures stay in the browser, no cookies, no personal data kept by the publisher; only an anonymous Clarity stability check.';
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} noindex={true}
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbSchema([{ name: label('home', lang), path: route('home', lang) }, { name: label('privacy', lang), path: route('privacy', lang) }])]}
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: label('privacy', lang) }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="lead">In short: the calculators send your salary and other figures nowhere, the site sets no cookies and the publisher records no personal data; the only processing is an anonymous technical stability check with Microsoft Clarity in cookie-free mode. Below are the details the General Data Protection Regulation (EU Regulation 2016/679) requires for {SITE_URL}.</p>

    <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>For data protection matters, write to the same address: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. No data protection officer has been appointed, as the GDPR does not require one at this scale of processing.</p>

    <h2>2. The calculators send nothing</h2>
    <p>Every calculation runs in your browser. Your gross salary, children, age, car or property details are <strong>not transmitted to any server</strong>, not stored and not linked to any identifier. There are no accounts and no sign-up.</p>
    <p>After you change a field, the calculator writes the values into the page address so you can share a ready-made calculation. The link itself does contain your figures and stays in your browser history, so only send it to people you want to see them; and if you open a link that already carries values, those values are part of the address of the page you visit.</p>

    <h2>3. What is actually processed</h2>
    <h3>Hosting provider logs</h3>
    <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Like any server, it receives the visitor’s IP address and technical request data on every visit; according to <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages/getting-started-with-github-pages/what-is-github-pages" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">GitHub’s documentation</a>, visitors’ IP addresses are logged and stored for security purposes. We have no access to those logs and do not use them. The legal basis is legitimate interest (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)): serving the page and protecting it from abuse.</p>
    <h3>Anonymous stability check with Microsoft Clarity, without cookies</h3>
    <p>The publisher records no personal data about visitors. To make sure the pages and calculators work, we use Microsoft Clarity, for which Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited (One Microsoft Place, South County Business Park, Leopardstown, Dublin 18, Ireland) is responsible, in cookie-free mode: before it loads, the site tells Clarity that cookies are not allowed, and Clarity sets none. For each page view it measures errors, load times, clicks that go nowhere and scrolling, without tying visits together; page text and whatever you type are masked. Microsoft receives the technical data of the request, including the IP address from which it infers an approximate location, and keeps recordings for 30 days and aggregated data for up to 13 months.</p>
    <h3>Legal basis and your right to object</h3>
    <p>The legal basis is our legitimate interest in a site that works properly (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)); no cookie or identifier stays on your device. You can object at any time by blocking the <code>clarity.ms</code> domain or writing to us. The site uses no other measurement or tracking tool. More on the <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies page</a>.</p>
    <h3>Emails</h3>
    <p>If you write to us, we process your address and message to reply and, where needed, to correct a calculation (GDPR art. 6(1)(f)). We keep correspondence for no more than three years after the last exchange.</p>
    <h3>Advertising</h3>
    <p>The site shows no advertising.</p>

    <h2>4. Who receives data</h2>
    <p>We do not sell, rent or share personal data. Recipients are the hosting provider, our mail provider for emails, and Microsoft for the technical data of the stability check.</p>

    <h2>5. Transfers outside the European Economic Area</h2>
    <p>GitHub, Inc. and Microsoft Corporation are based in the United States, so technical data may be processed outside the EEA. Microsoft Corporation is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework, and standard contractual clauses also apply; see the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft privacy statement</a>. If you block the clarity.ms domain, no transfer to Microsoft takes place.</p>

    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right of access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and objection to processing based on legitimate interest (GDPR arts. 15 to 21). Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>; we answer free of charge within one month. As we keep no user accounts, we usually hold nothing that identifies you beyond any correspondence, and we will tell you so plainly.</p>
    <p>You may also complain to a supervisory authority. The controller is established in France, so the lead authority is the {LEGAL.supervisoryAuthority} (<a href={LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl} rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">{LEGAL.supervisoryAuthorityUrl.replace('https://', '')}</a>). If you live in Greece you can also turn to the Hellenic Data Protection Authority (<a href="https://www.dpa.gr" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">dpa.gr</a>), under GDPR article 77.</p>

    <h2>7. No profiling</h2>
    <p>A calculator result is an operation you request, carried out on your device with your own data. It has no legal effect and is not an automated decision within the meaning of GDPR article 22. We build no user profiles.</p>

    <h2>8. Security and changes</h2>
    <p>The connection to the site is encrypted (HTTPS) and no user database is kept. Any new tool will be added to this page and to the cookies page before it is switched on. The terms of use are <a href={route('terms', lang)}>here</a>.</p>
    <p>Version of {updated}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
